            <li><strong>2000–2007:</strong> Steady foundation building and recovery from the early 2000s tech bust.</li>
            <li><strong>2008–2009:</strong> The Global Financial Crisis brought a significant correction, but recovery was swift.</li>
            <li><strong>2010–2021:</strong> A multi-year mega-bull run propelled by international expansion and the shift to high-margin DTC (Direct-To-Consumer) sales channels.</li>
            <li><strong>Post-2021:</strong> A period of normalization and increased volatility amid changing consumer dynamics, inflation, and macro headwinds.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Volatility and Risk Assessment -->
